FNFC-01.12 RX-miss probe v2 (temporary, NOT for commit). Applies on fnfc-01.11-fdt-t1 (e3b768c55).
  git apply nfc_dumps/pm3_parity/out/2026-10-13-fnfc0112/rx_miss_probe.patch
  ./fbt DEBUG=0 --extra-define=NFC_RX_MISS_PROBE FLIP_PORT=... flash_usb_full
One record per listener RxEnd, queued (non-blocking) right after the receiver is re-armed for the next frame and
printed by a Low priority thread (CLI `log info`). v1 printed from the worker itself: the USB log blocked the
worker for milliseconds, the signal reader ISR overran its 32-byte buffer and the Flipper rebooted.
  [P12] n=<RxEnd #> len=<rx bytes incl. CRC> b0/cmd/blk=<request bytes 0/1/10 (2 if short)> crc=<request CRC ok>
        tx=<replies sent>/<reply bytes> eof2dma=<request EOF (parser ISR) -> first reply DMA, us>
        txend2arm=<end of previous reply -> last (re)start of the signal reader before this frame, us>
        armed2sof=<that (re)start -> SOF pattern of this frame, us>
        fail2sof=<last spurious trigger (first byte not SOF) -> SOF of this frame, us>
        rearm=<end of this reply -> signal reader restarted for the next frame, us>  (H1 window)
        sofail=<triggers whose first byte was not SOF/EOF, since previous RxEnd> pfail=<invalid 1-of-4 symbol
        inside a frame> restarts=<parser restarts> maxrestart=<max Fail (ISR) -> restart (thread), us>
        ovf=<ISR found the 32-symbol buffer still full (thread too slow)> maxb=<max fill seen by ISR>
        wake=<max ISR "buffer full" -> thread parse, us> bad=<last offending byte> drop=<records lost (queue full)>
Remove with: git apply -R .../rx_miss_probe.patch

